\details{
The IBBA wrappers read the Israel Basketball Association's ASP.NET web service at
\code{basket.co.il/ws/ws.asmx} (the ops its own site calls): seasons, boards, teams, rosters,
coaches, schedules and results, box scores from 2004-05, season stats and leaders of the
Winner League (Israeli Premier League). They mirror sdv-py's
\code{sportsdataverse.basketball.ibba} wrappers of the same names: same arguments, the same
snake_case columns and types, one row per sdv-py row. The live box score, play-by-play and
shot coordinates of a game are in the \code{\link[=ibba_segev_game_info]{ibba_segev_game_info()}} family (Segev Stats).

\strong{Unofficial and unsupported.} The web service is keyless, unofficial and reverse
engineered. Requests are spaced at least one second apart per host (429 / 502 / 503 / 504
are retried three times; an HTTP 500 is the host's deterministic error page, a stack
trace, and is not retried); keep crawls slow and incremental. Contact details (e-mail,
phone, fax) and coaches' dates of birth are dropped.

\strong{Seasons and ids.} \code{season} is the END year and the host's own \code{cYear} (2026 = 2025-26):
it is sent unchanged. \code{team_id} and \code{player_id} are per-SEASON registrations (Maccabi Tel
Aviv = team 1109 in 2025-26, 2111 in 2026-27); the host has no cross-season person id (the
stable player key is the Segev player id of the \verb{ibba_segev_*()} family). \code{team_uid} is the
stable club id (Maccabi = 10). A \code{0} means "all" where an argument says so; every parameter
of an op is always sent.

\strong{Coverage.} League box scores from 2004-05 (\code{season = 2005}). \code{external_id} and
\code{segev_game_id} exist only from 2025-26 (earlier games carry no Segev id, so
\code{segev_game_id} is \code{NA}). The women's league and Liga Leumit are NOT on this host. Every
value on the wire is a string and Hebrew text is HTML-entity encoded: ids, counts and dates
are cast and text is unescaped.

\strong{Errors} are classed conditions, never a warning plus an empty frame: \code{hoopR_no_data}
(HTTP 404, an empty body, which is what an unknown id answers, or an empty row list),
\code{hoopR_bad_request} (HTTP 400 / 422, or an argument that is not a non-negative integer,
a boolean or a non-empty string as the op needs) and \code{hoopR_asset_fetch} (any other
failure: another status, a transport error, a body that is not JSON, an error or changed
envelope, a row for another season, team, player, board or game, or a box score of a game
that is not final). All inherit \code{hoopR_error}.
}
